  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "P300 dataset from initial spot study",
  "description": "An auditory oddball P300 EEG dataset from 13 healthy participants, recorded with 31 channels at 1000 Hz. Target (1000 Hz) and non-target (500 Hz) tones were presented at stimulus onset asynchronies from 60 to 600 ms. The dataset supports closed-loop optimization of stimulation speed in auditory brain-computer interfaces, using random search and Bayesian optimization to maximize regularized LDA classification performance.",
  "methods_description": "The experiment had an optimization part and a validation part. In the optimization part, four strategies (AUC-ucb, AUC-rand, P300-ucb, P300-rand) each had 20 minutes to find an optimal SOA. In the validation part, the resulting SOAs and a fixed 60 ms SOA were tested with 20 trials each. EEG was recorded with a BrainProducts BrainAmp DC and passive Ag/AgCl electrodes, referenced to the nose. Features were mean amplitudes in 5 time intervals across 31 channels and were classified with shrinkage rLDA using 13-fold cross-validation.",
